Venna_AI: Mastering the Shell with GitHub Copilot CLI

Prompt Used:
copilot -p "I committed locally but haven't pushed yet. I want to combine the last two commits into a single commit with a new message." --agent git

Copilot Response:
git rebase -i HEAD~2
# change second pick to squash
git reset --soft HEAD~2
git commit -m "feat: combine last two commits"
git push --force-with-lease

Screenshot: See copilot_screenshot.png

Accuracy Ranking: 9/10
Justification: Very accurate, correctly uses rebase -i HEAD~2 with squash and reset --soft alternative. Explains safety since not pushed yet. Optimizes workflow by staying in terminal.
